notes.body:
I think here we want to check for errors:

```
if (dissect_pkt_line(tvb, git_tree, &offset) != 0)
  return 0;
```

If we were calling in a loop, this would produce confusing behavior, since it would set `offset` to `0` each time. If you want to use a variable to store the result, can it be a different variable?

```
int result = dissect_pkt_line(tvb, git_tree, &offset);
if (result != 0)
  return 0;
```

I think even more readable would be to avoid the temporary variable:

```
if (dissect_pkt_line(tvb, git_tree, &offset) != 0)
  return 0;
```

Idea for a followup (i.e., not about this MR): it would be nice to check that we handled the entire tvbuff here. That is, something like

```c
if (offset != tvb_captured_length(tvb))
  proto_tree_add_expert(... explanation of the uncaptured part goes here ...)
return offset;
```

